    <figcaption>InterOcean Hotel and Northern Pacific park, 1908</figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<p>In 1896, the hotel moved its dining room to the former east parlor on the second floor, while the kitchen and pantries remained on the first. A new dumbwaiter carried meals upstairs.</p>

<p>{% person "r-b-hanna" %}R. B. Hanna{% endperson %} purchased the property in 1916 and renamed it the Lewis and Clark Hotel. The building was demolished the following year. A new {% place "lewis-and-clark-hotel" %}Lewis and Clark Hotel{% endplace %}, which remains standing, opened on the site in January 1918.</p>
